Track 1: Steal the Chalk, Hide the Square
- Story & Context: When water sensors tripped on the lower city grid, brass player Bram Thorne dragged a portable Prophet synth and his muted trumpet to the roof of the old rail terminal, playing improvisations over the sound of incoming emergency sirens. The night erupted into an impromptu gathering as dozens of displaced dwellers gathered in the rain, watching the water swallow their streets while the brass section built a terrifyingly gorgeous wall of sound. As the tide swallowed the final mark on the dock wall, Bram leaned into his microphone and sang, "Draw the line where the floor used to be, then leap before the chalk runs clear."
