- Story & Context: The final recording captured by Kjølen Drift before their rooftop generator was seized by coastal patrol officers, this track relies on ducking an entire orchestral string arrangement under the real-time audio feed of a warning flare horn. Local legend states that the song's closing quarter-tone trumpet solo actually induced a sympathetic resonance in the steel cables of the adjacent suspension bridge. The final line echoed across the water just as the power cuts: "When the red lights duck, we play the silence back to the sea."
